-- Update API Documentation built-in template to full detailed content.
UPDATE public.prd_templates
SET
  description = 'This template provides a comprehensive guide for documenting APIs, including purpose, functionalities, architecture, authentication, error handling, and endpoints.',
  structure = '{"instructions": "Write for the developer consuming the API, not the team that built it. Lead with working code examples in at least two languages. Error responses should include actionable troubleshooting steps. Authentication should have a copy-pasteable quickstart. Organize endpoints by what developers want to accomplish, not just by HTTP method.", "sections": [{"name": "API Overview", "guidelines": "High-level summary of the API.\n\n### Purpose\n- What the API does and the key problems it solves\n- Primary use cases and who the consumers are\n\n### Architecture\n- API style: REST, GraphQL, gRPC, WebSocket\n- Base URL and versioning strategy (e.g., `/api/v1/`)\n- Rate limiting and throttling policies\n- Data format: JSON, XML, protobuf\n\n### Core Capabilities\nList the main things developers can do with this API:\n- [Capability 1]: Brief description\n- [Capability 2]: Brief description\n- [Capability 3]: Brief description"}, {"name": "Authentication", "guidelines": "How developers authenticate with the API.\n\n### Methods\nFor each supported method:\n- Method: API Key / OAuth 2.0 / Bearer Token / etc.\n- Setup: Step-by-step instructions to get credentials\n- Usage: How to include credentials in requests (header, query param)\n\n### Quick Start\n\n```bash\ncurl -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN\" \\\nhttps://api.example.com/v1/resource\n```\n\n### Token Management\n- How to obtain and refresh tokens\n- Expiration policy\n- Secure storage best practices\n\n### Common Issues\n- [Error]: [Cause and fix]\n- [Error]: [Cause and fix]"}, {"name": "Endpoints", "guidelines": "Detailed reference for every API endpoint.\n\n### Format for Each Endpoint\n\n```text\nMETHOD /path\nDescription: What it does\nAuth: Required / Public\n\nParameters:\n- param (type, required/optional): Description\n\nRequest Body:\n{ field: type, field: type }\n\nResponse (200):\n{ field: type, field: type }\n\nError Responses:\n- 400: Invalid input — [details]\n- 401: Unauthorized\n- 404: Resource not found\n```\n\n### Grouping\nOrganize endpoints by resource or use case (e.g., Users, Projects, Billing), not just by HTTP method.\n\n### Pagination\nDescribe the pagination approach: cursor-based, offset, or page-number. Show request and response format."}, {"name": "Error Handling", "guidelines": "How errors are communicated and how to handle them.\n\n### Error Response Format\n\n```json\n{\n  \"error\": {\n    \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\",\n    \"message\": \"Email is required\",\n    \"details\": [...]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Error Code Reference\n| Code | HTTP Status | Description | Resolution |\n|------|-------------|-------------|------------|\n| VALIDATION_ERROR | 400 | Invalid input | Check request body |\n| UNAUTHORIZED | 401 | Missing or invalid token | Re-authenticate |\n| FORBIDDEN | 403 | Insufficient permissions | Check API key scopes |\n| NOT_FOUND | 404 | Resource doesn''t exist | Verify resource ID |\n| RATE_LIMITED | 429 | Too many requests | Back off and retry |\n| INTERNAL_ERROR | 500 | Server error | Retry; contact support if persistent |\n\n### Retry Strategy\n- Which errors are retryable (429, 500, 503)\n- Recommended backoff strategy (exponential with jitter)\n- Maximum retry attempts"}, {"name": "Code Examples", "guidelines": "Working examples in common languages.\n\n### cURL\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://api.example.com/v1/resource \\\n-H \"Authorization: Bearer TOKEN\" \\\n-H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n-d ''{\"name\": \"example\"}''\n```\n\n### JavaScript / TypeScript\n\n```typescript\nconst response = await fetch(''https://api.example.com/v1/resource'', {\n  method: ''POST'',\n  headers: {\n    ''Authorization'': ''Bearer TOKEN'',\n    ''Content-Type'': ''application/json'',\n  },\n  body: JSON.stringify({ name: ''example'' }),\n});\n```\n\n### Python\n\n```python\nimport requests\nresponse = requests.post(\n    ''https://api.example.com/v1/resource'',\n    headers={''Authorization'': ''Bearer TOKEN''},\n    json={''name'': ''example''},\n)\n```\n\nInclude examples for the most common use cases, not just basic CRUD."}, {"name": "Webhooks & Events", "guidelines": "If the API supports webhooks or event subscriptions.\n\n### Available Events\n- event.type: When it fires and what data it includes\n- event.type: When it fires and what data it includes\n\n### Webhook Setup\n- How to register a webhook endpoint\n- Payload format and signature verification\n- Retry policy for failed deliveries\n\n### Security\n- How to verify webhook signatures\n- IP allowlisting (if applicable)\n- Handling duplicate events (idempotency)\n\nIf webhooks are not applicable, describe any polling or streaming alternatives."}, {"name": "SDKs, Rate Limits & Support", "guidelines": "Practical information for developers integrating with the API.\n\n### SDKs & Libraries\n- Official SDKs: [Languages and install commands]\n- Community libraries: [Notable third-party options]\n- OpenAPI/Swagger spec URL for code generation\n\n### Rate Limits\n| Tier | Requests/min | Burst | Notes |\n|------|-------------|-------|-------|\n| Free | [limit] | [limit] | |\n| Pro | [limit] | [limit] | |\n| Enterprise | [limit] | [limit] | Custom |\n\n### Support & Resources\n- API status page URL\n- Developer documentation URL\n- Community forum or Discord\n- Support email or ticketing for escalations\n- Changelog / release notes URL"}]}'::jsonb
WHERE name = 'API Documentation' AND is_built_in = true;
